{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-deformed-commutator","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-deformed-commutator","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-deformed commutator $[\\hat{X}, \\hat{P}]_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-planck-constant","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"tags":["heisenberg","uncertainty","commutator","reeb","fibre-coordinate"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.qDeformedCommutator","text":"q-deformed-commutator.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-deformed-commutator.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-deformed-commutator\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{X}, \\hat{P}</code> be the position and momentum observables on the fibre <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J \\colon H \\to H</code> be the complex structure on the Levi distribution (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^2 = -\\mathrm{Id}</code>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in \\mathrm{End}(\\mathbf{1})</code> be the substrate parameter. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed commutator</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{X}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{P}</code> at a point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\in M</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  [\\hat{X}, \\hat{P}]_q := J\\,\\hbar_q(p),\n  \\qquad \\hbar_q(p) = 1 - q(p)^{-1},</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q</code> is the quantum Planck constant.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-deformed-commutator.md","heading":"Definition","number":"3.8.1"}
